{"name":"Queen’s Coat","hex":"#9d433f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"queen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wife, consort, or widow of a king.","A female monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act the part of a queen; to behave imperiously; to queen it.","To make a queen or (figuratively) to give the status of a queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen"},{"term":"coat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer garment covering the upper torso and arms.","A covering of material, such as paint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with a coating of some material.","To cover like a coat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coat","blocks":[{"text":"A coat is an outer garment for the upper body, worn by any gender for warmth or fashion. Coats typically have long sleeves and are open down the front, and closing by means of buttons, zippers, hook-and-loop fasteners, toggles, a belt, or a combination of some of these. Other possible features include collars, shoulder straps, and hoods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg/330px-FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mens_Coats_1872_Fashion_Plate.jpg/500px-Mens_Coats_1872_Fashion_Plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mens_Coats_1872_Fashion_Plate.jpg/500px-Mens_Coats_1872_Fashion_Plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Overcoat (left) and topcoat (right) from The Gazette of Fashion, 1872","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMens_Coats_1872_Fa